            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0630" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.113/362: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-25T13:00:00-06:00">August 25, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>148. Department’s telegram No. 50, August 17, 4 p.m. Note received today from
                    Ministry of Foreign Affairs acknowledging receipt of my communication informing
                    it of change in procedure for the issuance of licenses for exportation of arms
                    and munitions from the United States to Nicaragua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
